        "abstract": "Critical to design is the inclusion of components and design features to manage hazardous conditions. The art of design is balancing the associated risks of each hazard with an appropriate risk reduction action to optimize safety while minimizing unnecessary cost. When implemented effectively, these components and design features directly influence design, application, and manufacturing processes to yield a safer product and effective certification. This paper provides a process for quantifying risk and risk reduction methods highlighting benefits and commonly encountered certification challenges, ultimately aiding cost benefits. ",
